{{also|take out}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|take out}}
* {{l|en|take-out}}

===Etymology===
From the verb phrase ''take out''.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|North America}} (Of food) intended to be [[eaten]] off the [[premises]] from which it was bought.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|North America}} Food purchased from a [[takeaway]].
# {{lb|en|curling}} A [[stone]] that hits another stone, removing it from play.
# {{lb|en|bridge}} A double of an opponent's bid, intended to invite one's partner to compete in the auction, rather than to penalise one's opponents.

